verdicts.already_known:
Partly disclosed. ARCH §9 M0b "Carried-over model notes" (1), at docs/design/ARCHITECTURE.md:2189, already says Π resets only at ΣB_Q = 0. It proposes the same fix as Option B: "roll the Π epoch whenever lock_norm reaches 0". However, that note:
- says "Π telescopes to ≈ WAD·ΣB_Q/b_min", which holds only within a single lock era and ignores the compounding;
- covers only the u128 overflow consequence, not the loss of lock decay;
- judges it unreachable, assuming it needs inventory below about 5e-14 of b_min.

The multi-era compounding and the loss of decay at small Π are not disclosed in docs/AUDIT.md or the design docs.
